        "id": "p13-q4-shade-sum",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Add $\\frac{1}{8}$ to $\\frac{1}{4}$, represented on the diagram below, by shading.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [
          {
            "id": "p13-q4-eighths",
            "role": "question",
            "format": "tikz",
            "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"givenFill\",\"hex\":\"C7C7C7\",\"reason\":\"the supplied quarter is represented by two shaded eighths\"}],\"reference\":\"source page 13 p13-q4-eighths\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7.5mm,y=7.5mm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{givenFill}{HTML}{C7C7C7}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-0.14,-0.34) rectangle (8.14,1.55);\n\\fill[givenFill] (0,0) rectangle (2,0.6);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (0,0) rectangle (8,0.6);\n\\foreach \\i in {1,2,3,4,5,6,7}{\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (\\i,0)--(\\i,0.6);}\n\\foreach \\i in {2,4,6}{\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (\\i,-0.25)--(\\i,0.8);}\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (0,0.8)--(0,1)--(8,1)--(8,0.8);\n\\node[black,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,anchor=south] at (4,1.05) {1 whole};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
            "src": null,
            "widthMm": 65,
            "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
            "overlayOf": null,
            "transparent": false,
            "axes": null,
            "spec": {
              "sourcePage": 13,
              "sourceRegion": "Question 4, upper right fraction model",
              "description": "Eight equal cells, the first two shaded, with extended internal quarter divisions and a full-length bracket labelled 1 whole.",
              "mathematics": "The pre-shaded two eighths represent one quarter. The student adds one eighth by shading one further cell.",
              "answerVisibility": "Only the supplied one-quarter shading is visible."
            },
            "derived": false,
            "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
          }
        ],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Shade one more eighth. The total is $\\frac{3}{8}$.",
          "worked": "$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{8}&=\\frac{2}{8}+\\frac{1}{8}\\\\&=\\frac{3}{8}\\end{align*}$\nShade the third cell so that three of the eight cells are shaded.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p13-q4-eighths-solution",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"givenFill\",\"hex\":\"C7C7C7\",\"reason\":\"the initial two eighths represent the given quarter\"},{\"name\":\"addedFill\",\"hex\":\"D4E8FF\",\"reason\":\"the additional shaded eighth distinguishes the added quantity\"}],\"reference\":\"source page 13 p13-q4-eighths-solution\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7.5mm,y=7.5mm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{givenFill}{HTML}{C7C7C7}\n\\definecolor{addedFill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-0.14,-0.34) rectangle (8.14,1.55);\n\\fill[givenFill] (0,0) rectangle (2,0.6);\n\\fill[addedFill] (2,0) rectangle (3,0.6);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (0,0) rectangle (8,0.6);\n\\foreach \\i in {1,2,3,4,5,6,7}{\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (\\i,0)--(\\i,0.6);}\n\\foreach \\i in {2,4,6}{\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (\\i,-0.25)--(\\i,0.8);}\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (0,0.8)--(0,1)--(8,1)--(8,0.8);\n\\node[black,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,anchor=south] at (4,1.05) {1 whole};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 65,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
                "sourcePage": 13,
                "sourceRegion": "Question 4, upper right fraction model",
                "description": "The supplied two shaded eighths remain grey; a third eighth is shaded light blue.",
                "mathematics": "Two eighths plus one eighth equals three eighths.",
                "answerVisibility": "Completed shading appears only in the solution."
              },
              "derived": false,
              "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
            }
